  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nRiver valley fog has developed early this morning and will continue\nto expand across the riverbeds. Guidance suggests that overland fog \nwill be more limited as long as surface winds remain around 5 kts or \nso, but could have some transient fog develop in areas where winds go\nnearly calm. \n\nDrier air mass has settled into the region, with northeasterly flow \nin the lowest ~15000 ft of the atmosphere. This will result in more\nsunshine compared to the last few days. \n\nDrier air mass accompanied by seasonably cooler temperatures will\nremain intact through the weekend and into the beginning of next\nweek. Rain chances, along with a slight warming trend will return by\nthe middle of next week.",
